(2961809, 414334, 15711, '<td valign="top">Love the beautiful orangey yellow of the leaf. Nice detail on the veins. It tells a story, even without the title. I''d rotate, so that the bannister was more level. I''m sure it''s fine when you are just looking at it, but when it''s in an image, I keep turning, trying to straighten it out. LOL</td>', 'Love the beautiful orangey yellow of the leaf. Nice detail on the veins. It tells a story, even without the title. I''d rotate, so that the bannister was more level. I''m sure it''s fine when you are just looking at it, but when it''s in an image, I keep turning, trying to straighten it out. LOL', '2006-10-25 14:25:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2961811, 416800, 62318, '<td valign="top">Great context and title. I think I would have preferred a slightly sharper arm.</td>', 'Great context and title. I think I would have preferred a slightly sharper arm.', '2006-10-25 14:25:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2961817, 416920, 15711, '<td valign="top">I''m coming back to this and upping the score. I like that the bokeh is in the foreground AND background.  This is a touch more typical, but the colors are glorious.  I might crop out that blossom in the lower left. You could cut it tighter to the butterfly, and I don''t think it would hurt it. Best of luck. This is very pretty. 8</td>', 'I''m coming back to this and upping the score. I like that the bokeh is in the foreground AND background.  This is a touch more typical, but the colors are glorious.  I might crop out that blossom in the lower left. You could cut it tighter to the butterfly, and I don''t think it would hurt it. Best of luck. This is very pretty. 8', '2006-10-25 14:26:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(2961818, 417020, 66952, '<td valign="top">Really nice. It would be more effective if the entire front leaf was sharp.</td>', 'Really nice. It would be more effective if the entire front leaf was sharp.', '2006-10-25 14:26:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2961821, 414632, 29293, '<td valign="top">wow super bokeh but i wish the flower was closer to one of the colors in the background 9</td>', 'wow super bokeh but i wish the flower was closer to one of the colors in the background 9', '2006-10-25 14:26:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2961829, 416935, 5792, '<td valign="top">Hmmmm... I like the concept but the implementation doesn''t seem to work so well. I''m not trying to be harsh but will make some comments...<br/> <br/>I agree with the philosophy that an image with soft focused areas technically contains bokeh. But in a challenge about bokeh it needs to jump right out at you and say, "Now THAT''S bokeh!", otherwise it looks like any other soft focused image. Most good bokeh pictures are taken with the lens wide open for nice circular point light sources and with a shallow depth-of-field where the main subject is in sharp focus and the bokeh somehow highlights that main subject in a special way. All that is missing in your picture. That explains most of your low score.<br/> <br/>The overall technical quality is poor but I suspect that may have a lot to do with the camera you are using. You want to know your equipment''s limitations and work them to your advantage when possible.<br/> <br/>The shadow in the foreground is distracting to viewers. That destroys the whole idea of your picture. This needed to be taken at a different time when the shadow was not there and/or post processed in a way that adds pleasing attention to the shadowed area.<br/> <br/>This picture looks like it is strait out of the camera. That implies that you may be new to photography and/or unfamiliar with post processing. In the world of photography today you need to develop those skills. Fortunately, DPC is a good resource for helping you learn them.</td>', 'Hmmmm... I like the concept but the implementation doesn''t seem to work so well. I''m not trying to be harsh but will make some comments... I agree with the philosophy that an image with soft focused areas technically contains bokeh. But in a challenge about bokeh it needs to jump right out at you and say, "Now THAT''S bokeh!", otherwise it looks like any other soft focused image. Most good bokeh pictures are taken with the lens wide open for nice circular point light sources and with a shallow depth-of-field where the main subject is in sharp focus and the bokeh somehow highlights that main subject in a special way. All that is missing in your picture. That explains most of your low score. The overall technical quality is poor but I suspect that may have a lot to do with the camera you are using. You want to know your equipment''s limitations and work them to your advantage when possible. The shadow in the foreground is distracting to viewers. That destroys the whole idea of your picture. This needed to be taken at a different time when the shadow was not there and/or post processed in a way that adds pleasing attention to the shadowed area. This picture looks like it is strait out of the camera. That implies that you may be new to photography and/or unfamiliar with post processing. In the world of photography today you need to develop those skills. Fortunately, DPC is a good resource for helping you learn them.', '2006-10-25 14:28:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2961831, 414708, 67257, '<td valign="top">The colors make this picture great.</td>', 'The colors make this picture great.', '2006-10-25 14:29:41.000000', NULL, 1),
