(2967460, 416972, 61679, '<td valign="top">An interesting use of front bokeh.  I''m sure this unconventional approch isn''t getting the votes that it deserves, so I''ll give you a bonus point. 7</td>', 'An interesting use of front bokeh.  I''m sure this unconventional approch isn''t getting the votes that it deserves, so I''ll give you a bonus point. 7', '2006-10-27 08:59:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967464, 416482, 35602, '<td valign="top">Very pretty.  Like the smoothness of the drops.</td>', 'Very pretty.  Like the smoothness of the drops.', '2006-10-27 09:02:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967466, 416849, 35602, '<td valign="top">Too much in the image.  Need to limit the amount of elements you put in a composition.  The eye cannot comprehend so much as what is in  your image.</td>', 'Too much in the image.  Need to limit the amount of elements you put in a composition.  The eye cannot comprehend so much as what is in  your image.', '2006-10-27 09:04:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967476, 414954, 61679, '<td valign="top">Bumping to a 10.</td>', 'Bumping to a 10.', '2006-10-27 09:13:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967481, 416201, 61679, '<td valign="top">The essence of Bokeh.  Bumping to a 10</td>', 'The essence of Bokeh.  Bumping to a 10', '2006-10-27 09:15:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967505, 414168, 61679, '<td valign="top">Bumping to a 10.  Very nice work.</td>', 'Bumping to a 10.  Very nice work.', '2006-10-27 09:31:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967509, 417026, 61679, '<td valign="top">Bumping to a 10.  Very edgy (No pun intended).  The out of focus tower is so critical to this image for context.  Without it the image would be average.  Maybe not beautiful bokeh but very effective use of bokeh.</td>', 'Bumping to a 10.  Very edgy (No pun intended).  The out of focus tower is so critical to this image for context.  Without it the image would be average.  Maybe not beautiful bokeh but very effective use of bokeh.', '2006-10-27 09:34:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967513, 416027, 58728, '<td valign="top">You have some great bokeh here, but the flowers seem to be in a big shadow, which I feel takes away from the photo.  The foreground and background blend together, and it''s hard to find the focus point.  HOpe this helps.</td>', 'You have some great bokeh here, but the flowers seem to be in a big shadow, which I feel takes away from the photo.  The foreground and background blend together, and it''s hard to find the focus point.  HOpe this helps.', '2006-10-27 09:37:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967515, 413772, 58728, '<td valign="top">Such a creative title.  I love it.  The picture has great potential, but to me, the whole image looks a little out of focus.  I think it may have helped to turn the duck more to face the camera.  The wall in the background is also a bit distracting...but the colors and shadows above the wall are great. I wish the ducky was in front of that without the wall.  Hope this helps. Magen</td>', 'Such a creative title.  I love it.  The picture has great potential, but to me, the whole image looks a little out of focus.  I think it may have helped to turn the duck more to face the camera.  The wall in the background is also a bit distracting...but the colors and shadows above the wall are great. I wish the ducky was in front of that without the wall.  Hope this helps. Magen', '2006-10-27 09:40:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967518, 415228, 58728, '<td valign="top">I can see what you were going for here, but the image seems a bit busy.  I like the bokeh in the foreground, but the focal point in the image is super small, and I feel like I am having to strain to see it.  I think if you were in closer to the yellow flower it may have helped.  HOpe this helps you.</td>', 'I can see what you were going for here, but the image seems a bit busy.  I like the bokeh in the foreground, but the focal point in the image is super small, and I feel like I am having to strain to see it.  I think if you were in closer to the yellow flower it may have helped.  HOpe this helps you.', '2006-10-27 09:41:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967525, 416993, 57882, '<td valign="top">Well done.  Very elegant and awesome composition.</td>', 'Well done.  Very elegant and awesome composition.', '2006-10-27 09:48:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967546, 413926, 55956, '<td valign="top">greta eye or great luck :)</td>', 'greta eye or great luck :)', '2006-10-27 09:59:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967559, 413761, 55956, '<td valign="top">A fantastic image I think at the ribbon sure. 10</td>', 'A fantastic image I think at the ribbon sure. 10', '2006-10-27 10:04:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967581, 416852, 15711, '<td valign="top">I like the idea of this but..... I''m going to be a bit critical here. First, remove the frame. It doesn''t add to the shot and I think it''s too thin. I might put a wide black one around it if I left the orange (but most DPC people hate wide borders - so I get whacked for that all the time). I think it''s too busy.  The red leaves in the bottom are beautiful, but when you pile a rock, more leaves, more rocks and a pumpkin on it, it just gets too busy.  I''d have liked to just see the pumpin or maybe a leaf or two alone. I''d also not center the subject. The use of negative space gives the eye more of a place to go instead of being like a bullseye target in the middle of the shot. The bokeh is fine and I like that part very much, but I think instead of a subject, this has several and it makes it too hectic and is a tad contrived with them all stacked up like that. I hope you find this helpful. Many people complain that the mediocre scoring shots don''t get remarks, so I''m trying to respond to that complaint and give an honest opinion. ;~D</td>', 'I like the idea of this but..... I''m going to be a bit critical here. First, remove the frame. It doesn''t add to the shot and I think it''s too thin. I might put a wide black one around it if I left the orange (but most DPC people hate wide borders - so I get whacked for that all the time). I think it''s too busy.  The red leaves in the bottom are beautiful, but when you pile a rock, more leaves, more rocks and a pumpkin on it, it just gets too busy.  I''d have liked to just see the pumpin or maybe a leaf or two alone. I''d also not center the subject. The use of negative space gives the eye more of a place to go instead of being like a bullseye target in the middle of the shot. The bokeh is fine and I like that part very much, but I think instead of a subject, this has several and it makes it too hectic and is a tad contrived with them all stacked up like that. I hope you find this helpful. Many people complain that the mediocre scoring shots don''t get remarks, so I''m trying to respond to that complaint and give an honest opinion. ;~D', '2006-10-27 10:10:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967594, 415967, 15711, '<td valign="top">I like the idea of this and vivid berries really jump from the page.  What hurts it is the same thing that more than half of these images have: they are too busy.  In nature, there is alot going on, and unless you pluck, cut, remove, etc, you are stuck with alot of clutter and when shooting up close, it just all becomes a mass of this and that, instead of something to focus on. Then you add in the pattern of the bokeh (which is good by the way) and it just becomes confusing to the eye. If it were me, I would have either cut a piece of the bush off and hand held it away from the background, at a distance, to create the bokeh effect, OR strip the stem around just a few berries and a leaf or two, and do more of a macro. I hope this is helpful. :~D 5</td>', 'I like the idea of this and vivid berries really jump from the page.  What hurts it is the same thing that more than half of these images have: they are too busy.  In nature, there is alot going on, and unless you pluck, cut, remove, etc, you are stuck with alot of clutter and when shooting up close, it just all becomes a mass of this and that, instead of something to focus on. Then you add in the pattern of the bokeh (which is good by the way) and it just becomes confusing to the eye. If it were me, I would have either cut a piece of the bush off and hand held it away from the background, at a distance, to create the bokeh effect, OR strip the stem around just a few berries and a leaf or two, and do more of a macro. I hope this is helpful. :~D 5', '2006-10-27 10:14:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967600, 416894, 15711, '<td valign="top">Although this is well done, technical wise, it just isn''t very interesting.  When you shoot an image of an existing piece of art, sculpture, etc. it kind of takes away from the creativity for me, since somebody else has already done the subject matter. The lighting and bokeh are good. 5</td>', 'Although this is well done, technical wise, it just isn''t very interesting.  When you shoot an image of an existing piece of art, sculpture, etc. it kind of takes away from the creativity for me, since somebody else has already done the subject matter. The lighting and bokeh are good. 5', '2006-10-27 10:15:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967602, 416416, 51538, '<td valign="top">The light copper/gold background bokeh works well to enhance an already interesting photo. 8.</td>', 'The light copper/gold background bokeh works well to enhance an already interesting photo. 8.', '2006-10-27 10:16:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967603, 415951, 15711, '<td valign="top">I like the vivid colors and abstractness, but my first reaction (not to sound rude) is "oh, here we go with another image of glassware." I think if you didn''t crop out the bottom and give it that chopped off feeling, it might''ve been a bit more interesting.</td>', 'I like the vivid colors and abstractness, but my first reaction (not to sound rude) is "oh, here we go with another image of glassware." I think if you didn''t crop out the bottom and give it that chopped off feeling, it might''ve been a bit more interesting.', '2006-10-27 10:16:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967604, 416446, 67152, '<td valign="top">Nice shot - this really is an innovative way to use bokeh!</td>', 'Nice shot - this really is an innovative way to use bokeh!', '2006-10-27 10:16:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2967606, 416476, 67152, '<td valign="top">Nice shot - i like the background bokeh a whole bunch</td>', 'Nice shot - i like the background bokeh a whole bunch', '2006-10-27 10:17:11.000000', NULL, 1),
