(2989228, 416201, 16046, '<td valign="top">super composition, very well done.</td>', 'super composition, very well done.', '2006-11-02 13:16:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989230, 415234, 16046, '<td valign="top">Now that''s a 3D look, well done.</td>', 'Now that''s a 3D look, well done.', '2006-11-02 13:17:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989401, 416227, 30982, '<td valign="top">First, Ursula approved and that''s pretty much better than any higher score you might have achieved.  She''s the Queen of Bokeh.  I don''t limit "bokeh" to "circles of light" either.  It''s pretty much the way an OOF or soft background can highlight a subject - and you''ve done it well here.  The arch of the trees and the light space beneath them frame the young man quite nicely.  I don''t know about having to see his mouth or his smile - his eyes pass along an impishness that might not be seen as clearly otherwise.  And I do like the way the scarf seems way too big for him yet fails to contain his spirit.<br/> <br/>My only nit is a grayish horizontal line near the base of the picture - perhaps from a fence.  It does ever so slightly pull at the eye a bit.<br/> <br/>I took this into Photoshop and a bit more sharpening can be used to bring out the boy if you wish, but the softness doesn''t detract in my mind.</td>', 'First, Ursula approved and that''s pretty much better than any higher score you might have achieved.  She''s the Queen of Bokeh.  I don''t limit "bokeh" to "circles of light" either.  It''s pretty much the way an OOF or soft background can highlight a subject - and you''ve done it well here.  The arch of the trees and the light space beneath them frame the young man quite nicely.  I don''t know about having to see his mouth or his smile - his eyes pass along an impishness that might not be seen as clearly otherwise.  And I do like the way the scarf seems way too big for him yet fails to contain his spirit. My only nit is a grayish horizontal line near the base of the picture - perhaps from a fence.  It does ever so slightly pull at the eye a bit. I took this into Photoshop and a bit more sharpening can be used to bring out the boy if you wish, but the softness doesn''t detract in my mind.', '2006-11-02 13:55:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989452, 416935, 30982, '<td valign="top">Every once in awhile I think you throw one out there that possibly should have been simply thrown out, just to see what reaction you might get.  I do like the basic composition of this - the leading line through and out of the trees from the fork in the path, so to speak.  Has potential to be a pretty darn good shot, though I''d end it at the bottom of the light "v" - have the canopy of trees be the terminus.  Then you have the shiny bit of yellow and the opening near it up at the top of the picture, leading the viewer out and beyond.<br/> <br/>Technicals, however, are another story.  To my untrained and ignorant-of-finer-things eye, technicals pretty much suck, and in this case seriously detract from what could be a decent picture.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-11-02 14:10:31.</i></td>', 'Every once in awhile I think you throw one out there that possibly should have been simply thrown out, just to see what reaction you might get.  I do like the basic composition of this - the leading line through and out of the trees from the fork in the path, so to speak.  Has potential to be a pretty darn good shot, though I''d end it at the bottom of the light "v" - have the canopy of trees be the terminus.  Then you have the shiny bit of yellow and the opening near it up at the top of the picture, leading the viewer out and beyond. Technicals, however, are another story.  To my untrained and ignorant-of-finer-things eye, technicals pretty much suck, and in this case seriously detract from what could be a decent picture.', '2006-11-02 14:10:07.000000', '2006-11-02 14:10:31.000000', 0),
(2989505, 416935, 62095, '<td valign="top">I reckon this was far too harshly treated.  I didn''t vote on the challenge because I had my entry in it, but I''d likely have settled around the 6 mark on this one. Yeah, the shadow at the front is a tad distracting, and it would have been nice to have the focus dead sharp at the branch of the lines, but come on, that''s a great background / out of focus area that really complements the rest of the shot - the very essence of Bokeh.  <br/> <br/>In this challenge though, you obviously had to make all the voters go "ooo, shiny" in order to win big. Never mind that this has artistic watercolour quality to it.</td>', 'I reckon this was far too harshly treated.  I didn''t vote on the challenge because I had my entry in it, but I''d likely have settled around the 6 mark on this one. Yeah, the shadow at the front is a tad distracting, and it would have been nice to have the focus dead sharp at the branch of the lines, but come on, that''s a great background / out of focus area that really complements the rest of the shot - the very essence of Bokeh.   In this challenge though, you obviously had to make all the voters go "ooo, shiny" in order to win big. Never mind that this has artistic watercolour quality to it.', '2006-11-02 14:23:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989621, 416227, 38198, '<td valign="top">Cute guy! Good bokeh, subject stands out from the background, color mix is good. Had I voted it would have been a 7, only because the focus is somewhat soft on subject.</td>', 'Cute guy! Good bokeh, subject stands out from the background, color mix is good. Had I voted it would have been a 7, only because the focus is somewhat soft on subject.', '2006-11-02 15:03:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989709, 413515, 48115, '<td valign="top">WOW.. interessting voting going one here 90 x 1 thats unbelivably high! and 17 above 5 that to is unbelivable</td>', 'WOW.. interessting voting going one here 90 x 1 thats unbelivably high! and 17 above 5 that to is unbelivable', '2006-11-02 15:32:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989880, 416793, 42710, '<td valign="top">Now here''s something interesting. What are the chances of you and MrsKitty finding the exact same leaf with pretty much an exact same idea but with different colors? The leaf even has the same blemist at exact same location! Amazing!     <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=416476" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Flame on Fall!</a> <br/> <br/>Nice picture though. I like the green background better.<br/></td>', 'Now here''s something interesting. What are the chances of you and MrsKitty finding the exact same leaf with pretty much an exact same idea but with different colors? The leaf even has the same blemist at exact same location! Amazing!     Flame on Fall!  Nice picture though. I like the green background better.', '2006-11-02 16:15:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989885, 416476, 42710, '<td valign="top">Now here''s something interesting. What are the chances of you and fas-ligand finding the exact same leaf with pretty much an exact same idea but with different colors? The leaf even has the same blemist at exact same location! Amazing!     <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=416793" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Fall, a Tree''s Perspective</a> <br/> <br/>Nice picture though. I like the green background better.<br/></td>', 'Now here''s something interesting. What are the chances of you and fas-ligand finding the exact same leaf with pretty much an exact same idea but with different colors? The leaf even has the same blemist at exact same location! Amazing!     Fall, a Tree''s Perspective  Nice picture though. I like the green background better.', '2006-11-02 16:15:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989948, 413979, 30982, '<td valign="top">First off, it''s one heckuva shot and one heckuva find!  Great macro detail, lighting is spot on, colors are very good.  I like the fact there''s OOF in both the foreground and the background.  He''s pretty well camoflauged but the DOF used allows the viewer to "find" him.  That''s a pretty good use of "bokeh" to some extent, but a very sophisticated interpretation is required to see that.  The single flower near his head which is also in sharp focus (obviously it had to be) may be what limited the ability of the use of bokeh and/or DOF to bring out the bug more.<br/> <br/>There is some noise/grain in the background, but not enough to note.  Any picture with a shallow DOF will have noise/grain, and to me it''s normal.  I certainly don''t think it enough to seriously detract from your score but this is a very particular crowd!</td>', 'First off, it''s one heckuva shot and one heckuva find!  Great macro detail, lighting is spot on, colors are very good.  I like the fact there''s OOF in both the foreground and the background.  He''s pretty well camoflauged but the DOF used allows the viewer to "find" him.  That''s a pretty good use of "bokeh" to some extent, but a very sophisticated interpretation is required to see that.  The single flower near his head which is also in sharp focus (obviously it had to be) may be what limited the ability of the use of bokeh and/or DOF to bring out the bug more. There is some noise/grain in the background, but not enough to note.  Any picture with a shallow DOF will have noise/grain, and to me it''s normal.  I certainly don''t think it enough to seriously detract from your score but this is a very particular crowd!', '2006-11-02 16:33:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2989953, 416935, 55330, '<td valign="top">I think the darknes is metaforic and adds meaning to this piece.</td>', 'I think the darknes is metaforic and adds meaning to this piece.', '2006-11-02 16:34:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2990082, 415510, 56880, '<td valign="top">I really like the overlapping triangles of the butterfly wings and the flowers in the foreground; my eyes keep tracing around them.</td>', 'I really like the overlapping triangles of the butterfly wings and the flowers in the foreground; my eyes keep tracing around them.', '2006-11-02 17:02:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2990178, 415510, 11854, '<td valign="top">Great score on this one! I loved it!</td>', 'Great score on this one! I loved it!', '2006-11-02 17:24:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2990608, 414928, 22459, '<td valign="top">Hey doc! Congrats on the ribbon! Good to see you back, the place feels better already.</td>', 'Hey doc! Congrats on the ribbon! Good to see you back, the place feels better already.', '2006-11-02 19:00:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2990721, 416517, 45187, '<td valign="top">This is great.  Should have come higher than it did.  Tried so hard to do this but never managed.</td>', 'This is great.  Should have come higher than it did.  Tried so hard to do this but never managed.', '2006-11-02 19:19:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2990900, 415391, 30982, '<td valign="top">I thought I''d commented on this after the challenge but apparently did not.  This is lovely!!  Truly a very good use of bokeh, both in creating the watercolor effect and including "circles" to satisfy the bokeh police.  Composition is dead on - that second strand of grass behind is critical to this, in my opinion - nice balance.  And the way the colors fade from purple to a bit of blue to yellow/green is really, really nice.  Great job with this!</td>', 'I thought I''d commented on this after the challenge but apparently did not.  This is lovely!!  Truly a very good use of bokeh, both in creating the watercolor effect and including "circles" to satisfy the bokeh police.  Composition is dead on - that second strand of grass behind is critical to this, in my opinion - nice balance.  And the way the colors fade from purple to a bit of blue to yellow/green is really, really nice.  Great job with this!', '2006-11-02 19:48:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2991017, 414928, 2158, '<td valign="top">Amazing shot.  Congrats on the ribbon.<br/> <br/>Hope we''re going to see more of your work now.<br/> <br/>Oops - just noticed a few more of your recent entries.  My internet''s been behaving so badly lately, I''ve been missing everything.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-11-02 20:19:27.</i></td>', 'Amazing shot.  Congrats on the ribbon. Hope we''re going to see more of your work now. Oops - just noticed a few more of your recent entries.  My internet''s been behaving so badly lately, I''ve been missing everything.', '2006-11-02 20:14:18.000000', '2006-11-02 20:19:27.000000', 0),
(2991645, 415999, 66223, '<td valign="top">great photo... i like the flower, the bokeh, and love the bug!</td>', 'great photo... i like the flower, the bokeh, and love the bug!', '2006-11-02 22:49:40.000000', NULL, 0);
