(3011281, 414612, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Technical:  Color, saturation and hue are excellent.  Focus is nice and sharp.  <br/> <br/>Reaction:  The challenge is the background, and the background is beautiful.  However, the shadows on the leaves make them look as if they are damaged or dying.  On several of the leaves the shadows at first look like brown dead spots. <br/> <br/>When I look at the picture, I wonder what it might have looked like with only the single leaf that is broadside to the viewer.  That one makes a great contrast to the background.  As is, there is not really a single point of focus in the foreground to hold the eye for comparison against the background.<br/> <br/>Even so, I sure do love that background.  Nice work.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club Review: Technical:  Color, saturation and hue are excellent.  Focus is nice and sharp.   Reaction:  The challenge is the background, and the background is beautiful.  However, the shadows on the leaves make them look as if they are damaged or dying.  On several of the leaves the shadows at first look like brown dead spots.  When I look at the picture, I wonder what it might have looked like with only the single leaf that is broadside to the viewer.  That one makes a great contrast to the background.  As is, there is not really a single point of focus in the foreground to hold the eye for comparison against the background. Even so, I sure do love that background.  Nice work. ', '2006-11-07 17:54:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3011339, 417033, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Technical:  Color, saturation, hue:  Colors have been altered for effect, adding a bit of drama and coldness to the piece.  Fits the dead tree well.  Focus is very good.<br/> <br/>Reaction:  The trunk and background lights go against the idea of bokeh.  While the limbs and sky work well.  I''m not sure what you are trying to say with this piece.  The out of focus bulbs that jut out from the tree are distractions for me, while the out of focus bulbs that lie flatter, work better.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Technical:  Color, saturation, hue:  Colors have been altered for effect, adding a bit of drama and coldness to the piece.  Fits the dead tree well.  Focus is very good. Reaction:  The trunk and background lights go against the idea of bokeh.  While the limbs and sky work well.  I''m not sure what you are trying to say with this piece.  The out of focus bulbs that jut out from the tree are distractions for me, while the out of focus bulbs that lie flatter, work better.', '2006-11-07 18:26:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3011365, 415967, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Technical:  Color, saturation, and hue are good.  Focus is nice and sharp.  However, a shallower depth of field would have helped isolate the subject from the background.<br/> <br/>Reaction:  I really like the red berries and the amount of detail in each.  The leaves look a little wilted.  Was the branch cut earlier and placed there?  The leaves just look a little sickly.  The sky looks a little grainy, especially for an ISO of 80. The big thing is too much detail in the background.  A shallower depth of field would help a lot here to create the soft backgrounds normally associated with bokeh.  A larger f-stop would have helped here.  Not sure how wide the C-5000Z can go, but I would like to see this picture again, with a softer background.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Technical:  Color, saturation, and hue are good.  Focus is nice and sharp.  However, a shallower depth of field would have helped isolate the subject from the background. Reaction:  I really like the red berries and the amount of detail in each.  The leaves look a little wilted.  Was the branch cut earlier and placed there?  The leaves just look a little sickly.  The sky looks a little grainy, especially for an ISO of 80. The big thing is too much detail in the background.  A shallower depth of field would help a lot here to create the soft backgrounds normally associated with bokeh.  A larger f-stop would have helped here.  Not sure how wide the C-5000Z can go, but I would like to see this picture again, with a softer background.', '2006-11-07 18:39:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3016977, 414928, 27812, '<td valign="top">Please allow me to thank each and every one who liked this pic. <br/> <br/>To answer some questions...<br/> <br/>Yes it was a difficult subject to shoot, it is the first time ever I saw this insect and followed it around for about an hour. The Korean people thought I must be a mad man because I was running around, grunting,sweating and swearing like a sailor.But it was worth it for me, of the about 1Gig I shot I can use about 40 pics only.<br/> <br/>What made it so difficult is that this thing does not ''sit'' still long enough for autofocus. So later on I tried to anticipate it''s next flight plan, focussed manually and ...... became trigger happy.<br/> <br/>To share I have posted a few more on my portfolio. <br/> <br/>Thank you very much once again.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Please allow me to thank each and every one who liked this pic.  To answer some questions... Yes it was a difficult subject to shoot, it is the first time ever I saw this insect and followed it around for about an hour. The Korean people thought I must be a mad man because I was running around, grunting,sweating and swearing like a sailor.But it was worth it for me, of the about 1Gig I shot I can use about 40 pics only. What made it so difficult is that this thing does not ''sit'' still long enough for autofocus. So later on I tried to anticipate it''s next flight plan, focussed manually and ...... became trigger happy. To share I have posted a few more on my portfolio.  Thank you very much once again. ', '2006-11-09 08:06:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3017129, 416534, 31399, '<td valign="top">Nice job on the complementary colors and the vivid hues.  Perhaps it would help to cut/paste a humingbird drinking from the tumpet (lol, joking)  However, the DPC ''wow'' factor isn''t there I spose for the voters.  Perhaps a florist fake bumble bee placed in trumpet? lol</td>', 'Nice job on the complementary colors and the vivid hues.  Perhaps it would help to cut/paste a humingbird drinking from the tumpet (lol, joking)  However, the DPC ''wow'' factor isn''t there I spose for the voters.  Perhaps a florist fake bumble bee placed in trumpet? lol', '2006-11-09 09:24:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3019491, 416685, 66384, '<td valign="top">This was a really good idea. The only thing I can add to all the comments made during the challenge, is that I''d like to see how it would look with the position of two candies in the front reversed. I think that might balance the composition more, and give it a little more punch.</td>', 'This was a really good idea. The only thing I can add to all the comments made during the challenge, is that I''d like to see how it would look with the position of two candies in the front reversed. I think that might balance the composition more, and give it a little more punch.', '2006-11-10 07:01:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3021286, 415999, 50695, '<td valign="top">a memorable, unique photograph. I gave it a 7. you are on the right path. stay on it. there are two rules for staying on the path: do not think you are going the wrong way and do not think you are already home.</td>', 'a memorable, unique photograph. I gave it a 7. you are on the right path. stay on it. there are two rules for staying on the path: do not think you are going the wrong way and do not think you are already home.', '2006-11-10 23:42:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3021627, 416534, 55838, '<td valign="top">The background on this image rocks!  I love the color and bokeh - very nice!  I might have tried using selective colors to bring out the whites in the back even more (who knows) - but it''s awesome!  I think the poor score has nothing to do with the fine bokeh you captured but rather with the flower in the foreground.  As others have said, it is a bit washed out and could benefit from a tighter focus.  I think you could crop 1.5 to 2 inches off the right and make the flower seem more a part of the image too.  The color of the flower is beautiful against the gorgeous greens of the back.</td>', 'The background on this image rocks!  I love the color and bokeh - very nice!  I might have tried using selective colors to bring out the whites in the back even more (who knows) - but it''s awesome!  I think the poor score has nothing to do with the fine bokeh you captured but rather with the flower in the foreground.  As others have said, it is a bit washed out and could benefit from a tighter focus.  I think you could crop 1.5 to 2 inches off the right and make the flower seem more a part of the image too.  The color of the flower is beautiful against the gorgeous greens of the back.', '2006-11-11 08:35:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3021935, 417031, 66384, '<td valign="top">The clarity of the flower is fabulous. A strange effect is created by the drab background -- it looks like the flower is a fake paper cutout.</td>', 'The clarity of the flower is fabulous. A strange effect is created by the drab background -- it looks like the flower is a fake paper cutout.', '2006-11-11 13:54:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3022054, 415970, 66384, '<td valign="top">I added this to my favorites. I gave it a high score, but every time I see it I like it even more. The colors are beautiful, and I like the abstract feeling of the bokeh. To me, this is an perfect example of bokeh enhancing the image.</td>', 'I added this to my favorites. I gave it a high score, but every time I see it I like it even more. The colors are beautiful, and I like the abstract feeling of the bokeh. To me, this is an perfect example of bokeh enhancing the image.', '2006-11-11 15:02:03.000000', NULL, 0),
